{{Codex|Ring the death knell. Headshots briefly turn this scoped pistol into a rapid-fire, Critical Damage fiend that uses no ammo. When used by Harrow, Knell has a 2-round mag.}}

The '''Knell''' is {{WF|Harrow}}'s [[Signature Weapon|signature]] pistol that ultilizes its scope to more accurately land shots at long range. Although its magazine can only hold 1 round (2 rounds when equipped with Harrow), [[Enemy Body Parts|Weak Point Hits]] grant it [[Ammo Efficiency|infinite ammunition]] and increased [[critical multiplier]] and [[status chance]] for a short duration, making it a "high risk, high reward" weapon.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon primarily deals {{D|Puncture}} and {{D|Impact}} damage.
*Landing a successful Weak Point Hit grants the "'''Death Knell'''" buff, granting '''100%''' [[Ammo Efficiency]], increasing the final [[critical multiplier]] by '''+0.5x''' and increasing final [[status chance]] by '''20%'''. Buffs can stack up to '''3''' times, with each stack lasting '''2''' seconds and can be refreshed on subsequent Weak Point Hits. Stacks decay one at a time, each lasting the full '''2''' seconds.
*Precise at long range due to the scope feature.
**Scope can be used even in [[Bleedout]].
{{Advantages|
}}
{{Disadvantages|
*Can only load one shot at a time (two when used by {{WF|Harrow}}/{{WF|Harrow Prime}}).
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Knell Prime}}

==Acquisition==
The Knell's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*When used by {{WF|Harrow}} or {{WF|Harrow Prime}}, the Knell's magazine size is increased by '''1''' round, for a total of '''2''' rounds.
*'''Death Knell''' increases final [[critical multiplier]] by '''+0.5x''' and final [[status chance]] by '''+20%'''. It also grants unlimited ammo. The buff lasts for '''2''' seconds and can be refreshed.
**Critical multiplier and status chance bonus can stack up to '''3''' times. When the buff times out, one stack is lost and the buff duration resets.
**Critical multiplier bonus is calculated as:
**:{{MathText|Crit Multiplier {{eql}} 1.5 {{mul}} (1 + Crit Damage Mods) + 0.5 {{mul}} Number of Stacks}}
**The buff triggers on [[Enemy Body Parts|weak points]] (however, some exceptions include the backpacks of some [[MOA]] variants). Shooting weak points generated by either {{A|Sonar}} or {{M|Detect Vulnerability}} will also trigger the buff.
**Weak Point Hits on corpses can proc Death Knell.
**Individual [[Multishot]] bullets can proc Death Knell and can generate max stacks instantly from a single shot.
**As an indication that this buff is active, the scope design while zoomed in will evolve, as well as showing the '''Death Knell''' buff in the UI.
***The scope shows a 1.5x, 2.0x or 2.5x crit multiplier for the number of stacks respectively. However this does '''not''' represent the actual buff.

==Tips==
*While the text specifies headshots, the buffs also trigger off of Weak Points, such as [[Rogue Culverin]]'s arm canisters, [[Lumbering Fragment]]'s midpoint, and [[The Anatomizer]]'s midpoint.
*Synergizes well with {{A|Magnetize}}, {{Weapon|Scourge}}, {{WF|Harrow}}, {{Arcane|Arcane Precision}}, {{Arcane|Arcane Awakening}}, all other "On Weak Point" arcanes, {{M|Hydraulic Crosshairs}}, {{Weapon|Orvius}} and {{A|Prowl}} (only if using {{M|Suppress}}). This is due to it having a fast reload, extremely small magazine, and the focus on scoring headshots.
**Harrow's {{A|Condemn}}, in particular, synergizes extremely well with Knell as chained enemies leave their heads very vulnerable to being shot at.
**{{Weapon|Scourge}} also works particularly well with Knell, as the Bullet Attractor-like fields caused by throwing the speargun are created over the enemies' ''heads'', and make it easier to land headshots.
**Orvius' charged attack holds enemies in the air where they are open to headshots.
**Combining a maxed {{M|Primed Pistol Gambit}} with a maxed active {{M|Hydraulic Crosshairs}} will give a combined 322% crit chance bonus, bringing crit chance for the Knell to 84.4%. Using {{M|Galvanized Crosshairs}} instead at maximum stacks will increase this further to 507% crit chance bonus, boosting the total crit chance to 121.4% for guaranteed critical hits.
*Works surprisingly well in conjunction with {{WF|Nyx}}'s {{A|Mind Control}}, as headshots on the controlled enemy will still trigger Death Knell, but they will not take damage until the ability ends. This way you can always have a big-headed-buddy of your choice nearby for easy activations.
*{{M|Pressurized Magazine}} can be very beneficial on this weapon, as it will increase the fire rate during the infinite ammo buff considerably if you can score a Weak Point Hit quickly after reloading.
*{{M|Seeker|Seeker}} is also a viable mod for this pistol, especially when expecting enemies to spawn in a corridor such as the main hallway in a Void [[Defense]] mission, or when trying to score a headshot against an enemy hiding behind cover or [[Shield Lancer]]s.

==Trivia==
*A ''knell'' is the sound made by a bell, specifically when rung to signify a death or a funeral.
*When viewed from overhead Knell resembles a cross, possibly in reference to {{WF|Harrow}}'s priest/exorcist theme.
*There is Tennobet engraved at the bottom of Knell's handle. This translates to "KUHT", which could mean "Cut".

